        <!-- PHASE 1: DENMARK -->\
        <h2 class="section-title title-dk">\uc0\u55356 \u56809 \u55356 \u56816  Phase 1: Copenhagen, Denmark (11\'9616 October)</h2>\
\
        <!-- DAY 1 -->\
        <div class="day-card denmark">\
            <div class="day-header">\
                <span>DAY 1: Sunday, 11 October \'97 Flight Departure</span>\
                <span>Taipei \uc0\u8594  Transit</span>\
            </div>\
            <div class="day-body">\
                <ul class="timeline">\
                    <li><span class="time-tag">22:50</span> Parents depart Taipei Taoyuan Airport (T1) on China Airlines CI073 to Amsterdam[cite: 2].</li>\
                </ul>\
            </div>\
        </div>\
\
        <!-- DAY 2 -->\
        <div class="day-card denmark">\
            <div class="day-header">\
                <span>DAY 2: Monday, 12 October \'97 Arrival & N\'f8rrebro Base</span>\
                <span>Copenhagen</span>\
            </div>\
            <div class="day-body">\
                <ul class="timeline">\
                    <li><span class="time-tag">07:40</span> Parents land in Amsterdam (AMS) for 2 hr 45 min transit[cite: 2].</li>\
                    <li><span class="time-tag">09:35</span> Ya Wen lands at Copenhagen Airport (CPH) on flight FR5070[cite: 2].</li>\
                    <li><span class="time-tag">11:50</span> Parents land at CPH Terminal 3 on flight SK552[cite: 2]. Rendezvous in Arrival Hall[cite: 2].</li>\
                    <li><span class="time-tag">13:00</span> Transit to Airbnb via Metro (M2 to N\'f8rreport) or Taxi (Taxa 4x35)[cite: 2]. Drop luggage (Check-in 15:00)[cite: 2].</li>\
                    <li><span class="time-tag">15:30</span> <strong>First Exploration:</strong> Walk around the trendy N\'f8rrebro neighborhood[cite: 2] and Torvehallerne Glass Market.</li>\
                    <li><span class="time-tag">18:00</span> <span class="tag tag-food">RECOMMENDED DINNER</span> <strong>Hallernes Sm\'f8rrebr\'f8d</strong> inside Torvehallerne for traditional Danish open-faced sandwiches[cite: 2].</li>\
                </ul>\
                <div class="meta-box">\
                    <strong>\uc0\u55356 \u57313  Stay:</strong> N\'f8rrebrogade 13, 2200 Copenhagen (2nd floor)[cite: 2].\
                </div>\
            </div>\
        </div>\
\
        <!-- DAY 3 -->\
        <div class="day-card denmark">\
            <div class="day-header">\
                <span>DAY 3: Tuesday, 13 October \'97 Classic Copenhagen Must-Sees</span>\
                <span>Copenhagen</span>\
            </div>\
            <div class="day-body">\
                <ul class="timeline">\
                    <li><span class="time-tag">09:30</span> <span class="tag tag-mustsee">MUST SEE</span> <strong>Nyhavn Canal:</strong> Explore the iconic colorful harbor houses and historic wooden ships.</li>\
                    <li><span class="time-tag">10:30</span> <span class="tag tag-mustsee">MUST SEE</span> <strong>Classic Canal Tour:</strong> 1-hour boat cruise departing from Nyhavn through Copenhagen's harbor and canals.</li>\
                    <li><span class="time-tag">12:30</span> <span class="tag tag-food">RECOMMENDED LUNCH</span> <strong>Caf\'e9 Atelier September:</strong> Famous stylish local caf\'e9 known for whipped ricotta toast and exceptional coffee.</li>\
                    <li><span class="time-tag">14:30</span> <span class="tag tag-mustsee">MUST SEE</span> <strong>Amalienborg Palace & Marble Church:</strong> See the royal winter residence and the impressive dome.</li>\
                    <li><span class="time-tag">16:30</span> <span class="tag tag-mustsee">MUST SEE</span> <strong>The Round Tower (Rundet\'e5rn):</strong> Climb the spiral ramp for 360\'b0 panoramic views of the city center. Grab a snack at <em>D\'f8p Organic Hotdogs</em> right next door[cite: 2].</li>\
                    <li><span class="time-tag">19:00</span> <span class="tag tag-food">RECOMMENDED DINNER</span> <strong>H\'f6st:</strong> Exceptional New Nordic restaurant featuring Nordic wood aesthetics and seasonal local produce[cite: 2].</li>\
                </ul>\
            </div>\
        </div>\
\
        <!-- DAY 4 -->\
        <div class="day-card denmark">\
            <div class="day-header">\
                <span>DAY 4: Wednesday, 14 October \'97 Castles, Gardens & Hygge</span>\
                <span>Copenhagen</span>\
            </div>\
            <div class="day-body">\
                <ul class="timeline">\
                    <li><span class="time-tag">09:30</span> <span class="tag tag-mustsee">MUST SEE</span> <strong>Rosenborg Castle & King\'92s Garden:</strong> View the Danish Crown Jewels inside the Renaissance castle.</li>\
                    <li><span class="time-tag">12:00</span> <span class="tag tag-food">RECOMMENDED LUNCH</span> <strong>Aamanns Replik:</strong> High-end contemporary Sm\'f8rrebr\'f8d located near the Royal Theatre.</li>\
                    <li><span class="time-tag">14:00</span> <span class="tag tag-mustsee">MUST SEE</span> <strong>The Little Mermaid & Kastellet:</strong> Walk through the star-shaped fortress to see Denmark's most famous statue.</li>\
                    <li><span class="time-tag">16:30</span> <span class="tag tag-food">CAF\'c9 STOP</span> <strong>Democratic Bakehouse:</strong> Taste the absolute best almond croissants and fresh filter coffee in Copenhagen.</li>\
                    <li><span class="time-tag">18:30</span> <strong>Family Self-Catering Evening:</strong> Pick up fresh fish and Danish butter from Netto/Irma[cite: 2] and cook a cozy meal at the apartment[cite: 2].</li>\
                </ul>\
            </div>\
        </div>\
\
        <!-- DAY 5 -->\
        <div class="day-card denmark">\
            <div class="day-header">\
                <span>DAY 5: Thursday, 15 October \'97 Art & Historic Tivoli</span>\
                <span>Copenhagen</span>\
            </div>\
            <div class="day-body">\
                <ul class="timeline">\
                    <li><span class="time-tag">10:00</span> <strong>Day Excursion Option:</strong> Take a 35-minute coastal train north to <strong>Louisiana Museum of Modern Art</strong> (world-class seaside sculpture park).</li>\
                    <li><span class="time-tag">13:00</span> <span class="tag tag-food">RECOMMENDED LUNCH</span> <strong>Torvehallerne Food Hall:</strong> Try <em>\'c6bleskiver</em> (warm pancake balls)[cite: 2] and fresh juice.</li>\
                    <li><span class="time-tag">15:30</span> <span class="tag tag-mustsee">MUST SEE</span> <strong>Christiansborg Palace:</strong> Visit the Danish Parliament, Royal Reception Rooms, and the free tower view.</li>\
                    <li><span class="time-tag">18:00</span> <span class="tag tag-mustsee">MUST SEE</span> <strong>Tivoli Gardens:</strong> Explore the world\'92s second-oldest amusement park, beautifully illuminated with autumn lights.</li>\
                </ul>\
            </div>\
        </div>\
\
        <!-- PHASE 2: ICELAND -->\
        <h2 class="section-title title-is">\uc0\u55356 \u56814 \u55356 \u56824  Phase 2: Iceland South Coast Driving Tour (16\'9625 October)</h2>\
\
        <!-- DAY 6 -->\
        <div class="day-card iceland">\
            <div class="day-header">\
                <span>DAY 6: Friday, 16 October \'97 Flight to Iceland & Arrival</span>\
                <span>CPH \uc0\u8594  KEF \u8594  Reykjav\'edk (Drive: 50 km / 45 mins)</span>\
            </div>\
            <div class="day-body">\
                <ul class="timeline">\
                    <li><span class="time-tag">12:30</span> Arrive at CPH Airport T3 for flight SAS SK2595[cite: 2].</li>\
                    <li><span class="time-tag">15:25</span> Fly Copenhagen (CPH) \uc0\u8594  Iceland Keflav\'edk (KEF)[cite: 2].</li>\
                    <li><span class="time-tag">16:45</span> Land at KEF Airport[cite: 2]. Clear customs and collect luggage.</li>\
                    <li><span class="time-tag">17:30</span> <strong>Car Rental Pickup:</strong> Collect 4x4 vehicle from <em>Blue Car Rental</em>[cite: 2].</li>\
                    <li><span class="time-tag">18:00</span> \uc0\u55357 \u57042  <strong>CRITICAL Grocery Stop:</strong> Stock up at <strong>B\'f3nus Supermarket</strong> near KEF airport (Buy geothermal cucumbers, mini peppers, Skyr yogurts, butter, snacks)[cite: 2].</li>\
                    <li><span class="time-tag">19:30</span> Check into Reykjav\'edk Airbnb[cite: 2]. Relaxed casual evening in the capital city.</li>\
                </ul>\
                <div class="meta-box">\
                    <strong>\uc0\u55356 \u57313  Stay:</strong> S\'f6rlaskj\'f3l 12, 107 Reykjav\'edk[cite: 2].<br>\
                    <strong>\uc0\u55357 \u56983  Driving:</strong> 50 km (Keflav\'edk Airport to Reykjav\'edk Center).\
                </div>\
            </div>\
        </div>\
\
        <!-- DAY 7 -->\
        <div class="day-card iceland">\
            <div class="day-header">\
                <span>DAY 7: Saturday, 17 October \'97 Capital Sights & Journey to Glass Lodge</span>\
                <span>Reykjav\'edk \uc0\u8594  Seljalandsfoss \u8594  Hella (Drive: 120 km / 1 hr 40 mins)</span>\
            </div>\
            <div class="day-body">\
                <ul class="timeline">\
                    <li><span class="time-tag">09:30</span> <span class="tag tag-mustsee">MUST SEE</span> Walk through downtown Reykjav\'edk: See <strong>Hallgr\'edmskirkja Church</strong> and the <strong>Harpa Concert Hall</strong> waterfront.</li>\
                    <li><span class="time-tag">12:00</span> <span class="tag tag-booked">PRE-BOOKED DINING</span> <strong>Old Iceland Restaurant:</strong> Reserved lunch slot![cite: 2] Excellent traditional fish and lamb (Laugavegur 72)[cite: 2].</li>\
                    <li><span class="time-tag">14:00</span> Drive South along Route 1 toward Hella[cite: 2]. Optional stop at <em>Raufarh\'f3lshellir Lava Tunnel</em> or <em>Keri\'f0 Crater</em>[cite: 2].</li>\
                    <li><span class="time-tag">16:00</span> <span class="tag tag-booked">HIGHLIGHT STAY</span> Check into <strong>Panorama Glass Lodge</strong> (Alva / Room 1 & 2)[cite: 2].</li>\
                    <li><span class="time-tag">18:00</span> Enjoy the glass ceiling views, private hot tub, and shared sauna session[cite: 2]. Nighttime Northern Lights hunting from bed!</li>\
                </ul>\
                <div class="meta-box">\
                    <strong>\uc0\u55356 \u57313  Stay:</strong> Panorama Glass Lodge, Austurkr\'f3kur 1, 851 Hella[cite: 2].<br>\
                    <strong>\uc0\u55357 \u56983  Driving:</strong> 120 km total driving time.\
                </div>\
            </div>\
        </div>\
\
        <!-- DAY 8 -->\
        <div class="day-card iceland">\
            <div class="day-header">\
                <span>DAY 8: Sunday, 18 October \'97 Horse Riding & Geothermal Greenhouse</span>\
                <span>Hella & Golden Circle Region (Drive: 90 km / 1 hr 15 mins)</span>\
            </div>\
            <div class="day-body">\
                <ul class="timeline">\
                    <li><span class="time-tag">10:00</span> Morning coffee in the glass lodge[cite: 2]. Drive toward Reykjadalur[cite: 2].</li>\
                    <li><span class="time-tag">11:30</span> <span class="tag tag-food">RECOMMENDED LUNCH</span> <strong>Fri\'f0heimar Tomato Farm:</strong> Dine inside a warm geothermal tomato greenhouse! Famous all-you-can-eat tomato soup and fresh sourdough bread[cite: 2].</li>\
                    <li><span class="time-tag">13:30</span> <span class="tag tag-booked">PRE-BOOKED TOUR</span> <strong>S\'f3lhestar Horse Riding:</strong> 1.5-hour Icelandic horse riding experience through Reykjadalur Valley[cite: 2].</li>\
                    <li><span class="time-tag">16:00</span> <span class="tag tag-mustsee">MUST SEE</span> <strong>Geysir Geothermal Area & Gullfoss Waterfall:</strong> Watch Strokkur erupt every 6-10 minutes.</li>\
                    <li><span class="time-tag">18:30</span> Return to Panorama Glass Lodge for second luxury night[cite: 2]. Cook lighter self-catering dinner[cite: 2].</li>\
                </ul>\
                <div class="meta-box">\
                    <strong>\uc0\u55356 \u57313  Stay:</strong> Panorama Glass Lodge, Hella[cite: 2].\
                </div>\
            </div>\
        </div>\
\
        <!-- DAY 9 -->\
        <div class="day-card iceland">\
            <div class="day-header">\
                <span>DAY 9: Monday, 19 October \'97 Waterfalls, Black Sands & Journey East</span>\
                <span>Hella \uc0\u8594  Vik \u8594  \'d6r\'e6fi (Drive: 270 km / 3 hrs 30 mins)</span>\
            </div>\
            <div class="day-body">\
                <ul class="timeline">\
                    <li><span class="time-tag">09:00</span> Check out of Hella[cite: 2]. Drive East along Ring Road 1[cite: 2].</li>\
                    <li><span class="time-tag">09:30</span> <span class="tag tag-mustsee">MUST SEE</span> <strong>Seljalandsfoss & Sk\'f3gafoss:</strong> Walk behind Seljalandsfoss and admire the massive power of Sk\'f3gafoss.</li>\
                    <li><span class="time-tag">12:30</span> <span class="tag tag-food">RECOMMENDED LUNCH</span> <strong>The Soup Company (Vik):</strong> Try their famous signature <em>Red Lava Soup</em> served in a dark sourdough bowl[cite: 2].</li>\
